 anchorCtr="0" anchor="ctr" bIns="45700" lIns="91425" spcFirstLastPara="1" rIns="91425" wrap="square" tIns="45700"><a:noAutofit/></a:bodyPr><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:pPr indent="0" lvl="0" marL="0" marR="0" rtl="0" algn="ctr"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:srgbClr val="2FB0DC"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPts val="4000"/><a:buFont typeface="Calibri"/><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr b="1" i="0" lang="en-US" sz="4000" u="none" cap="none" strike="noStrike"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="2FB0DC"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>Transport Across Membranes</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:cxnSp><p:nvCxnSpPr><p:cNvPr id="523" name="Google Shape;523;p71"/><p:cNvCxnSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvCxnSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="457200" y="838200"/><a:ext cx="8229600" cy="0"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="straightConnector1"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln cap="flat" cmpd="thinThick" w="57150"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="2FB0DC"/></a:solidFill><a:prstDash val="solid"/><a:miter lim="800000"/><a:headEnd len="med" w="med" type="none"/><a:tailEnd len="med" w="med" type="none"/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:cxnSp><p:pic><p:nvPicPr><p:cNvPr descr="An image depicting the movement of solutes across a permeable membrane.&#xA;Image (a) has two cylinders. The first is labeled as C1 &gt;&gt; C2, and is the before equilibrium net flux. The cylinder is split in half vertically. On the left is C1, and has orange dots interspersed throughout. On the right is C2, which has nine orange dots. A very thick blue arrow moves from C1 to C2. Another less thick arrow moves from C2 to C1. The right cylinder is C1 equals C2 and show at equilibrium net flux. The orange dots in this cylinder are spread equally throughout the C1 and C2 sides. The arrows, as described above, are also equal. Image (b) has two cylinders. Both are split in half. The first shows Vm &gt; 0 before equilibrium. On the left is a black negative. It has most negative circles and one positive circle. On the right side is a red positive. This has mostly positive red pluses in circles and one negative in a circle. It has a thich red arrow pointing from the positive side to the negative side. It has a thing black arrow pointing the same way. It also has a thick black arrow going from the negative side to the positive side. It also has a thin red arrow pointing the same way. The right cylinder is Vm equal 0 and is at equilibrium. Both sides of this cylinders are equal with positive and negative circles throughout. The four arrows are also all the same size." id="524" name="Google Shape;524;p71"/><p:cNvPicPr preferRelativeResize="0"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvPicPr><p:blipFill rotWithShape="1"><a:blip r:embed="rId3"><a:alphaModFix/></a:blip><a:srcRect b="0" l="0" r="0" t="0"/><a:stretch/></p:blipFill><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="2019300" y="4038600"/><a:ext cx="5219700" cy="2800350"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln><a:noFill/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:pic></p:spTree></p:cSld><p:clrMapOvr><a:masterClrMapping/></p:clrMapOvr></p:sld>